{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<iostream>\n#include<algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\nusing llong = long long;\nconst llong MOD = 1000000007;\n\nllong fastPow(llong base, llong exp, llong mod) {\n    llong result = 1;\n    base %= mod;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % mod;\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nllong modPow(llong base, llong exp) {\n    return fastPow(base, exp, MOD);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    llong p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    \n    if (k % p == 1) {\n        cout << modPow(p, p);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    if (k % p == 0) {\n        cout << modPow(p, p - 1);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    llong order = 1;\n    while ((p - 1) % order != 0 || fastPow(k, order, p) != 1) {\n        order++;\n    }\n    \n    cout << modPow(p, (p - 1) / order);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n\n    public static long fastPow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base %= mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    public static long modPow(long base, long exp) {\n        return fastPow(base, exp, MOD);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long p = scanner.nextLong();\n        long k = scanner.nextLong();\n        \n        if (k % p == 1) {\n            System.out.println(modPow(p, p));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        if (k % p == 0) {\n            System.out.println(modPow(p, p - 1));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        long order = 1;\n        while (((p - 1) % order != 0) || (fastPow(k, order, p) != 1)) {\n            order++;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(modPow(p, (p - 1) / order));\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001408954558428377, -2.622600959512056e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.30981186684221e-05, -3.671578815556131e-05, -0.001263297046534717, -0.10320829600095749, -1.585470999998506e-05, -5.4596363042946905e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.682172998902388e-05, -0.0011709030950441957, -2.1934269170742482e-05, -0.9119254946708679, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -1.168244216387393e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.4318398573086597e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.9141146923357155e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.622600959512056e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.01884976588189602, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.16026391088962555, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -8.761498611420393e-05, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -8.201262971851975e-05, -7.390948667307384e-06, -4.768370